								<div class="playerBiography">
									Almost no sound emanated from the darkness that hung over the Lesser Faydark.  A young dark elf walked quietly through the trees, avoiding any creatures that might be hiding about.  Barely visible, he went unnoticed by a band of brownies that ran past him.  They seemed to be rushed, as if they were after something.  After a moment he could sense the source of the brownies’ curiosity.  Racing ahead of them, he came upon a gathering of brownies.  They were chasing the little elf and moving in closer to her.  One of the brownies moved a little and Vikular was able to see the elf.  She was a very small high elf child, obviously frightened and running as fast as she could.  She had a small club clenched in her hands so hard that her little knuckles were turning white.  Mud and leaves were caked all over her face and hair.  Eventually the brownies started surrounding her; there was no place for her to run.  Everyone, including Vikular was surprised when she turned around and bravely held her ground.  Her lip quivered a bit, but she stood there holding that club ever tighter.  
Vikular could tell that the little elf wasn’t going to win this battle.  He took pity on her and grabbed her.  Running as fast as a bard can run, he took her to Castle Mistmoore.  Once inside they were safe from the brownies, but many more dangers lurked inside the castle for the little elf.  All of this action was just too much for her and she passed out in his arms.  He took her to the basement of the castle, carefully avoiding running into any of the creatures that hung around in the darkness nearby.  Vikular had lived in the basement of the castle most of his life.  The rogues that raised him had disappeared one day quite some time ago.  He feared they might have died raiding Felwithe or the likes.  He left the little elf in his bed while he ventured to the Lesser Faydark in hopes of finding some sign of her parents.  He found places where there had been an obvious struggle, but no sign of the high elves that had so stupidly brought their child to this place.
When he returned to the castle, she was still sleeping.  He sat near her the entire night and watched her sleep until at last he fell asleep himself.  In the morning he awoke to find her staring at him.  He wasn’t sure how she’d react to him; he doubted she’d ever even seen a dark elf.  Apparently she knew that he had saved her, for although she was a little timid and dared not approach him, she did not seem to fear him.  Vikular suddenly felt very awkward with this child looking at him with her big bright eyes.  He looked at her for a moment and muttered something about food as he left the room.  When he returned, he handed her a plate with some rolls on it and a flask of water.  Her eyes were so sad, that he soon realized that she knew of her parents’ demise, and asked her no questions.  The only thing she said to him the entire day was her name, Amyana.
The following weeks were hard for her, and she became quickly attached to her savoir.  She followed him everywhere he went, afraid to be left alone.  Even at night, she slept next to him, with her little fingers twisting themselves around in his hair.  Amyana had taken to calling Vikular her father shortly after they met and seemed to forget about her parents completely.  He knew that her parents had begun raising her in the ways of a cleric of a Tunare.  It was quite obvious when, at night she would ask Tunare to bless him.  Sensing that she’d be a wonderful cleric, he continued the training she’d started.  Of course, he was a bard of hate himself, and taught her loyalty to him as well as to Tunare.
Making ends meet was hard enough however, and they weren’t able to purchase any armor for the young cleric. They found their solution in Yeolarn Bronzeleaf. He sent Amyana on a hunt, and agreed that upon her return, he would give her some armor to wear. Every day for two weeks, Amyana set out into the Faydwer searching for the items Yeolarn had asked for. The search was exasperating, but she was almost finished. Late one evening, she was hunting down a mature Aborean (a large tree-like beast) when she came across a ranger and a necromancer, Noetikos and Valerene. They offered to help Amyana track down the Arborean. She seemed somewhat nervous with them at first, nonetheless, she was gracious to her new companions, and followed them through the Faydwer. The ranger was a wood elf, and although much older than the younger women accompanying him, he was by no means old, especially not in elven terms. The three of them got along well, and eventually he invited the young cleric to join a guild. This is how Amyana became a member of Binded Souls. 
It was also during this time that the guild Jade Dragon began to rise up to become, once again, a force to be reckoned with. This was the guild to which Vikular belonged.  Vikular rose to power within Jade Dragon and was spending less and less time near the Castle Mistmoore.  His relationship to Amyana was secret still, and although it saddened him to see her go, he was glad she’d found a guild to join.  
The leader of Binded Souls, Rikov was a lively little frog. He grew to like the young elf, and promoted her within his ranks. Amyana spent the next few months traveling, and under the tutelage of Valerene she became a bit of a baker. She let the adventurer in her guide her ways. She came to have many friends in her new guild, and she loved them each dearly. Ayteyex accompanied her on many adventures, porting the little elf all over Norrath, as druids do. Panddabear let her follow him around, keeping him safe as he explored places such as the Field of Bone. Uanelil followed her faithfully as well, helping her with the many rezes that clerics do. These three, along with Noetikos quickly became her closest friends. 
It was not long before whispers began of her origins.  Uanelil sought Vikular out one evening.  The necromancers from the Castle where they had lived, had told several people of the odd family, and thus the secret was out.  Grateful for Uanelil’s discretion, Vikular called for Amyana. They had not seen each other in a long time, and Vikular was almost surprised to see how she’d grown.  Her loyalties remained, as always, to Tunare and to Vikular.  They visited for a long time, discussing how this new development would affect them.  In the end, the times in Norrath had changed so much that it mattered very little to anyone.  There would be always be a few stares here and there, but there was no real reason to hide it anymore.  
Things continued much as they were for a time, with both guilds growing well, until one day, Rikov vanished. Nobody heard from him for a long time, and people were thinking of leaving Binded Souls. In order to keep the guild together as much as possible, Amyana created Moonlite Redemption. Many members of Binded Souls followed her to this new guild. Among the last to leave was Noetikos, his decision was a hard one, as he felt loyalty to both Rikov and Amyana. 
Rikov did return, but only to find that his guild was a whisper of what it had once been. Eventually, Rikov disbanded Binded Souls, and came to join Moonlite Redemption. Shortly thereafter, Amyana and Noetikos came to be co-leaders of Moonlite Redemption. They complimented each other well as leaders, as they did as friends as well, until the day came for Noetikos to move on. Amyana still leads Moonlite Redemption, and the guild grows stronger and larger with each passing day.  Although Vikular has followed his own path, and his own guild, he still makes time to see, and help, his little elf.  
The story ends not here, for there shall be many more a year.

In Felwithe, Issynal struggled to make ends meet, eventually allowing Amyana to sell her baked goods.  Amyana was a dreamer, her thoughts were constantly being distracted by dreams of grandeur.  She found the merchant life boring, and dreamt of better things.  

Amyana planned to leave Felwithe one day, and she figured that the first step would be to learn to fight.  Her mother agreed, thinking it was good for a young lady to be able to defend herself should the need arise.  Making ends meet was hard enough however, and they weren’t able to purchase any armor for the young cleric.  They found their solution in Yeolarn Bronzeleaf .  He sent Amyana on a hunt, and agreed that upon her return, he would give her some armor to wear.

Every day for two weeks, Amyana set out into the Faydwer searching for the items Yeolarn had asked for.  The search was experating, but she was almost finished.  Late one evening, she was hunting down a mature Aborean (a large tree-like beast) when she came across a ranger and a necromancer.  They offered to help Amyana track down the Arborean.  A young high elf, Amyana had never seen a dark elf before, and the necromancer’s appearance was somewhat unsettling to her.  Nonetheless, she was gracious to her new companions, and followed them through the Faydwer.  

The ranger was a wood elf, and although much older than the younger women accompanying him, he was by no means old, especially not in elven terms.  The three of them got along well, and eventually he invited the young cleric to join a guild.  This is how Amyana became a member of Binded Souls.  The leader of Binded Souls, Rikov was a lively little frog.  He grew to like the young elf, and promoted her within his ranks. 

Amyana spent the next few months traveling.  She let the adventurer in her guide her ways.  In the back of her heart, she hoped she would find her father.  She came to have many friends in her new guild, and she loved them each dearly.  Ayteyex accompanied her on many adventures, porting the little elf all over Norrath, as druids do.  Panddabear let her follow him around, keeping him safe as he explored places such as the Field of Bone.  Uanelil followed her faithfully as well, helping her with the many rezes that clerics do.  These three, along with Noetikos quickly became her closest friends.

One day, Rikov vanished.  Noone heard from him for a long time, and people were thinking of leaving Binded Souls.  In order to keep the guild together as much as possible, Amyana created Moonlite Redemption.  Many members of Binded Souls followed her to this new guild.  Among the last to leave was Noetikos, his decision was a hard one, as he felt loyalty to both Rikov and Amyana.  Rikov did return, but only to find that his guild was a whisper of what it had once been.  Eventually, Rikov disbanded Binded Souls, and came to join Moonlite Redemption.

Eventually, Amyana and Noetikos came to be co-leaders of Moonlite Redemption.  They complimented eachother well as leaders, as they did as friends as well, until the day came for Noetikos to move on.  Amyana still leads Moonlite Redemption, and the guild grows stronger and larger with each passing day.  

Amyana still makes time to visit Felwithe to see her mother.  Vivicia has joined Moonlite Redemption, and makes time to stop in whenever she has a moment, which is rare anymore.  

The preceeding hath been a recounting of the life of Amyana Angeluv.  As her life hath yet to end, more may accompany this detailing in the near future.


